{"entities":[{"text":"lipid","label":"Chemical","id":""},{"text":"NS-718","label":"Chemical","id":""},{"text":"amphotericin B","label":"Chemical","id":""},{"text":"NS-718","label":"Chemical","id":""},{"text":"amphotericin B","label":"Chemical","id":""},{"text":"NS-718","label":"Chemical","id":""},{"text":"Fungizone","label":"Chemical","id":""},{"text":"amphotericin B-sodium deoxycholate","label":"Chemical","id":""},{"text":"D-AmB","label":"Chemical","id":""},{"text":"amphotericin B","label":"Chemical","id":""},{"text":"NS-718","label":"Chemical","id":""},{"text":"D-AmB","label":"Chemical","id":""},{"text":"urea","label":"Chemical","id":""},{"text":"creatinine","label":"Chemical","id":""},{"text":"D-AmB","label":"Chemical","id":""},{"text":"NS-718","label":"Chemical","id":""},{"text":"D-AmB-treated","label":"Chemical","id":""},{"text":"NS-718-treated","label":"Chemical","id":""},{"text":"Amphotericin B","label":"Chemical","id":""},{"text":"NS-718-treated","label":"Chemical","id":""},{"text":"D-AmB-treated","label":"Chemical","id":""},{"text":"amphotericin B","label":"Chemical","id":""},{"text":"lipid","label":"Chemical","id":""},{"text":"NS-718","label":"Chemical","id":""},{"text":"amphotericin B","label":"Chemical","id":""},{"text":"nephrotoxicity","label":"Disease","id":""},{"text":"tubular necrosis","label":"Disease","id":""},{"text":"nephrotoxicity","label":"Disease","id":""}],"entity_aliases":[{"text":"lipid","id":"1","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"NS-718","id":"2","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"NS-718-treated","id":"2","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"D-AmB","id":"3","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"Fungizone","id":"3","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"D-AmB-treated","id":"3","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"Amphotericin B","id":"3","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"amphotericin B","id":"3","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"amphotericin B-sodium deoxycholate","id":"3","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"urea","id":"4","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"creatinine","id":"5","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"nephrotoxicity","id":"1","label":"Disease"},{"text":"tubular necrosis","id":"1","label":"Disease"}],"filtered_entities":[{"text":"lipid","id":"1","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"NS-718-treated","id":"2","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"amphotericin B-sodium deoxycholate","id":"3","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"urea","id":"4","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"creatinine","id":"5","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"tubular necrosis","id":"1","label":"Disease"}],"gold_relations":"D-AmB | CID | tubular necrosis","labels":"Chemical,Disease","metrics":{"precision":1.0,"recall":1.0,"f1":1.0,"tp":1,"fp":0,"fn":0,"rel_precision":1.0,"rel_recall":1.0,"rel_f1":1.0,"rel_tp":1,"rel_fp":0,"rel_fn":0},"pairs":[{"head":"lipid","tail":"tubular necrosis","head_id":"1","tail_id":"1"},{"head":"NS-718-treated","tail":"tubular necrosis","head_id":"2","tail_id":"1"},{"head":"amphotericin B-sodium deoxycholate","tail":"tubular necrosis","head_id":"3","tail_id":"1"},{"head":"urea","tail":"tubular necrosis","head_id":"4","tail_id":"1"},{"head":"creatinine","tail":"tubular necrosis","head_id":"5","tail_id":"1"}],"relations":["3 | 1"],"text":"Attenuation of nephrotoxicity by a novel lipid nanosphere (NS-718) incorporating amphotericin B. NS-718, a lipid nanosphere incorporating amphotericin B, is effective against pathogenic fungi and has low toxicity. We compared the toxicity of NS-718 with that of Fungizone (amphotericin B-sodium deoxycholate; D-AmB) in vitro using renal cell cultures and in vivo by biochemical analysis, histopathological study of the kidney and pharmacokinetic study of amphotericin B following intravenous infusion of the formulation in rats. Incubation with NS-718 resulted in significantly less damage of cultured human renal proximal tubular epithelial cells compared with D-AmB. Serum blood urea and creatinine concentrations increased significantly in rats given an iv infusion of D-AmB 3 mg/kg but not in those given the same dose of NS-718. Histopathological examination of the kidney showed tubular necrosis in D-AmB-treated rats but no change in NS-718-treated rats. Amphotericin B concentrations in the kidney in NS-718-treated rats were higher than those in D-AmB-treated rats. Our in vitro and in vivo results suggest that incorporation of amphotericin B into lipid nanospheres of NS-718 attenuates the nephrotoxicity of amphotericin B."}